AB  - Managing stable pH levels within bioreactors remains a continuous challenge owing to time-variant behaviour, inherent uncertainty, and non-linear system dynamics. The challenge is even greater in such bioprocesses, especially Saccharomyces cerevisiae culturing for invertase production, since the pH needs to be tightly controlled in the process. Often, a standard proportional-integral (PI) controller struggles to follow the titration curve and achieve the desired setpoint. This work presents the hybrid control study between the Adaptive Neuro-Fuzzy Inference System (ANFIS) and the Winer model-based PI controller in solving the problem. The adaptive neuro-fuzzy PI controller significantly enhances control performance through minimal overshoot and faster setpoint convergence, with smooth responses, as demonstrated by both simulation and real-time experimental validation. Really, the accuracy improved when the Integral Square Error (ISE) decreased from 2.4573 to 1.1067.  © 2025 IEEE.
