AB  - The objective of this work was to study the application of fuzzy logic control systems in comparison with conventional control systems for neutralization reactors employing pH measurement. A simulation program was developed for strong acid neutralization reactors, which are those that present the greatest problems related to automatic control based on this measurement. The goodness of the model was verified by comparison with experimental titration curves. Conventional and diffuse logic control strategies were proposed and applied using simulations, studying their responses to excitations. The diffuse logic treatment gave better responses and provided greater management flexibility.
